## El Capitan reverse-engineering decision

Do not add a whole-driver El Capitan decompilation project to the critical
path. ath9k explicitly names AR9565/0036; OCLP's AirPortAtheros40 inventory
lists 0030 and older devices, not 0036. That inventory is not a complete
silicon-support proof, and a 0030 spoof proves no AR9565 compatibility.
[ath9k identity definitions](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/hw.h),
[OCLP device inventory](https://github.com/dortania/OpenCore-Legacy-Patcher/blob/main/opencore_legacy_patcher/datasets/pci_data.py).

Use Ghidra/static disassembly only for a specific unanswered ABI/lifetime
question, prioritizing the exact 25G332 binary. State the question and the
observation needed to answer it; do not treat decompiled pseudocode as original,
complete source or mix it into the new driver. If needed, put curated findings
in reference/ and scratch binaries/projects/output in .temp/reference/.
No bulk reconstruction, copied legacy stack or additional archive is required.

## Evidence

- Source commits, reference URLs/version/rights, static review and lint diagnostics.
- Theoretical completeness only; no kext build, device scan, packet logs or hardware claims.
- Add offline host tests only where material behavior/error paths warrant them;
  run through tools/validate.py --tests without treating them as hardware proof.

## Native rel32 source-hardening checkpoint, 2026-11-09

`NativeProfile.hpp::findNativeLink` now rejects native-pattern mapping ranges
that cross `UINTPTR_MAX` and signed RIP-relative import targets that would
underflow/overflow `uintptr_t`. Previously, a synthetic negative displacement
from a low address matched an unrelated high import (pre-fix host exit 2).
`tests/test_relocate_safety.cpp` covers valid forward/backward rel32 targets
and three distinct wraparound cases with offline C++14/C++17 host execution.
This guards bounded source parsing; it does not establish that the private
Tahoe native class layout, symbol export eligibility or patch offsets match
25G332, and this P0 TODO remains open.
